WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
- Her new Showtime
documentary is called Sheryl.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.320
So what was it like to look back

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.180
at your life and your
career in this documentary,

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.890
was it kind of scary or weird?

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.960
- I think for me,

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.390
obviously I have like 30
years of my own career

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.760
and then I had a whole life before that.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.650
I think people forget,
especially with social media

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.480
and stuff, that we're people,

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.460
and that behind the artistry

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.490
and the drive to be an artist,

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.410
there's a world of challenges in there

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:29.100
that made you want to
reveal your vulnerabilities

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.250
and write music and were
really quick to judge.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.100
And so when Showtime came to me

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:35.983
and said do you wanna do documentary?

00:00:35.983 --> 00:00:38.340
I was like, absolutely not.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.173
- Yeah.

00:00:39.173 --> 00:00:41.220
- And then I kind of warmed up to the idea

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.640
of telling the story about
the person, as opposed to

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.350
the person that wrote "All I Wanna Do"

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.480
and "Soak Up The Sun".

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.515
- 'Cause those are different
chapters of us, you know?

00:00:50.515 --> 00:00:51.348
- They are.

00:00:51.348 --> 00:00:53.820
And your big hits don't
necessarily represent who you are.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.653
- Yeah.

00:00:54.653 --> 00:00:56.310
- They give you an opportunity
to go out into the world

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:57.360
and play your songs.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.310
But it's the deep cuts that really,

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:00.360
tell the story.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.530
It's been an interesting thing

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:04.200
and I hope people when
they watch it feel inspired

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.550
and they feel like, oh okay, yeah,

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.610
I've gone through depression
or I've had, you know,

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.610
sexual harassment in my life or, you know,

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.130
or I'm getting old, and what
does that mean in my career?

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.030
You know, that kind of thing.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.310
There's all kinds of challenges
that we all go through

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.660
whether you're famous or you're not.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.700
So, and that's what it's about.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.280
- Was there anything, because
this happens to me sometimes

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.080
it's only been 20 years
for me, but I just mean,

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.510
it happens to where
somebody will say something

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:30.000
and I'll be like, oh my God,
like, was there anything

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.250
in the documentary that you were like,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.870
surprised you about yourself?

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.053
Or like what happened
or you didn't remember.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:38.530
Okay. I wanna know what's happening.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.990
Okay. I wanna know. I wanna know.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.004
I wanna know, you don't lie,

00:01:41.004 --> 00:01:43.173
I wanna know what's happening right now.

00:01:44.065 --> 00:01:46.890
- This is total vanity.
I mean, it's so stupid.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:47.790
- I'm so excited.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:48.810
- First let me just preface it,

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.940
by saying that my kids say, mom, you know

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.383
you were born in the 1870s.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.193
- All our kids think we're old.

00:01:55.193 --> 00:01:56.700
- I know. And when I watched it,

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.093
I was like, oh my God, I'm so old.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.430
- No, I do see pictures,

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.860
and I'm like, oh, for me, like, I'm like

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.900
I see pictures, and I'm like, oh my God.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.310
- Like, oh, you're not. You're not.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.143
- I don't even care.

00:02:09.143 --> 00:02:11.580
- But that's the thing,
I don't usually care.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.020
But when you're watching yourself, like

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.410
on a camera speaking,
you're like, oh my God

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:17.970
my mouth is so ugly.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:21.090
Or then why am I making that
facial expression, you know.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.470
- You're known mouth.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.537
People love your mouth.

00:02:23.537 --> 00:02:25.170
Like's so funny.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.003
- They do?

00:02:26.003 --> 00:02:27.120
- You're like known for it.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.950
- Did you love that?

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.240
- No, but you're no, that's

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.670
like one of your things, what
it's so see, this is why.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:33.679
Okay. So I don't watch.

00:02:33.679 --> 00:02:34.512
- You can't watch yourself.

00:02:34.512 --> 00:02:35.345
- I don't watch myself.

00:02:35.345 --> 00:02:36.178
I don't watch interviews.

00:02:36.178 --> 00:02:37.770
I don't watch any, I don't watch myself.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:40.800
I don't or any articles that
review anything like that

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.540
because I think it changes you.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.030
And I think the things
that people love about you,

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.020
you'll change them.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.190
And that's what people love.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:48.023
So do you do that?

00:02:48.023 --> 00:02:49.220
Do you read anything?

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.160
- No, I don't. Since my second record.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.790
I've not read one single thing.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.530
I don't want people to tell me.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.840
I like being there.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.010
Feel good about it.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.810
And then I don't want somebody to,

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.330
yeah, rob me of that by
telling me that it wasn't good.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.460
And sometimes I'll be, I'll
be like that wasn't very good.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.600
But I'll own that.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.993
I just don't want somebody
else telling me their opinion.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.730
- Stay on your own front porch, sir.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.893
- Exactly. Who asked you?

